    "body": "Once you accept or decline cookies, the bar minimizes to below the Github logo and repository name in the footer on the bottom left. It appears to look like a design element of the footer, and it is not obvious that you should hover it it to expand it and click to launch.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"197\" alt=\"Screenshot 2020-11-18 at 12 22 07\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/114116/99525314-ed208a80-2999-11eb-9790-b9554a4ed490.png\">\r\n\r\nI see it works the same way on eclipse.org, so it is by design. And the fix might not be here, but in the cookie module being used. However I thought I would call it out anyway.",
